,title,link,text,language,family
0,Wanggamala language - Wikipedia,https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Wanggamala_language,"Wanggamala, also spelt Wanggamanha, Wangkamahdla, Wangkamadla, Wangkamanha, Wangkamana, Wonkamala, Wongkamala, Wonkamudla, and other variants, is an extinct Australian Aboriginal language of the Pama–Nyungan family, previously spoken in the Northern Territory around Hay River (east of Alice Springs) and to the south of the Andegerebinha ...",Wanggamala,Australian
1,Wanggamala - Wikipedia,https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Wanggamala,"The Wanggamala people, also spelt Wangkamahdla, Wangkamadla, Wangkamanha, Wangkamana, Wonkamala, Wongkamala, Wonkamudla, and other variants, are an Aboriginal Australian people of the Northern Territory and Queensland.",Wanggamala,Australian
2,Wangga - Wikipedia,https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Wangga,"March 13, 2026 - Wangga (sometimes spelled Wongga) is an Aboriginal Australian genre of traditional music and ceremony which originated in Northern Territory and north Western Australia, specifically from South Alligator River south east towards Ngukurr, south to the Katherine and west into the Kimberley.",Wanggamala,Australian
3,Indigenous music of Australia - Wikipedia,https://en.m.wikipedia.org/wiki/Indigenous_music_of_Australia,"1 week ago - The traditional forms include many aspects of performance and musical instrumentation that are unique to particular regions or Aboriginal Australian groups; and some elements of musical tradition are common or widespread through much of the Australian continent, and even beyond.",Wanggamala,Australian
4,Wanggamala language explained,https://everything.explained.today/Wangkamanha_language/,"Wanggamala, also spelt Wanggamanha, Wangkamahdla, Wangkamadla, Wangkamanha, Wangkamana, Wonkamala, Wongkamala, Wonkamudla, and other variants, is an extinct Australian Aboriginal language of the Pama–Nyungan family, previously spoken in the Northern Territory around Hay River (east of Alice Springs) and to the south of the Andegerebinha ...",Wanggamala,Australian
5,Timeless Aboriginal Melodies | Music of the Australian LandWanggamala ExplainedWanggamala - docs.verbix.comContext 12272: Wanggamala (Source: Australasia and the ...,https://www.youtube.com/watch?v=gYkUg37tdx0,"Jun 5, 2025 · Experience the spirit of the Australian land through Timeless Aboriginal Melodies, a collection of traditional sounds that echo the ancient wisdom of the First Nations people. The Wanggamala people, also spelt Wangkamahdla, Wangkamadla, Wangkamanha, Wangkamana, Wonkamala, Wongkamala, Wonkamudla, and other variants, are an Aboriginal Australian people of the Northern Territory and Queensland. Note on Australian languages with no known speakers: For some languages, we haven't been able to confirm speaker numbers. In other cases, there isn't anyone who has grown up speaking the language, but there are still people who identify with the language, and who are working to revitalize their languages. Wanggamala Login To Join The Community Suggest A Change Also Known As: Tharlimanha, Wanggamanha, Wangkamala, Wangkamana, Wangkamanha, Wonggaman, Wonggawan, Wongkamala, Wonkamala, Wonkamudla, Wangkamadla Dialects & Varieties Explore Revitalization Program Locate Wanggamala Overview Info Resources Members Revitalization Events Online Communities ...",Wanggamala,Australian
